Subject: [DRAFT] AI COLUMN: add __all_ai_column and __all_ai_column_task inner table definitions

NOT COMPILED, NOT RUN. This machine has no Linux toolchain and the inner-table
schema is a build-time generated artifact (src/share/inner_table/
generate_inner_table_schema.py, invoked from CMakeLists.txt:38). After applying
this hunk you must re-run the generator and rebuild; nothing here was verified.

Column names below are not a free design choice: every one of them is referenced
by the shipped acceptance tests on origin/2026-competition, so the names are hard
requirements:

  oceanbase.__all_ai_column(table_id, column_id, column_name, state_column_id,
      request_column_id, result_spec_column_id, max_retries, normalized_expr)
      <- tools/deploy/mysql_test/test_suite/ai_column/t/ai_column_ddl.test:39-78
  oceanbase.__all_ai_column_task(table_id, rowkey_predicate, request_id, state,
      retry_count, eligible_ts)
      <- .../t/ai_column_t1_dml.test:32-37,101-106,151-156
      <- .../t/ai_column_worker.test:42-47,95-101
      <- .../t/ai_column_vector_index.test:58-63,109-114

Rowkey choice for the task table: (table_id, request_id, column_id) makes the
"one request group per row/change, one task row per AI column" assertion
(count(*) = 2 and count(distinct request_id) = 1) structurally true rather than
something the DML path has to remember to uphold.

table_id 1131/1132 are unused on this ref (only 1128/1129/1130 for the AI model
tables and 1133/1134 for __all_objauth_mysql are taken in that range; grep for
'113[12]' and '113[5-9]' in the def file returns nothing).

