Notes for whoever applies this:
  1. `OB_MAX_SERVER_NAME_LENGTH` and `OB_MAX_TYPE_NAME_LENGTH`-style constants
     must be confirmed to exist in src/share/ob_define.h; `OB_MAX_ERROR_MSG_LEN`
     and `OB_MAX_COLUMN_NAME_LENGTH` are proven in use by
     __all_vector_index_task (def line 2349-2394) and __all_column (def line
     316). Replace any unproven constant with a literal length before running
     the generator.
  2. Each new system table also needs its `oceanbase.__all_ai_column` /
     `__all_ai_column_task` read views (the tests query them through
     `oceanbase.`), modelled on the __all_vector_index_task views at def lines
     13706 and 13739.  Those view definitions are not included here because
     they must be generated against the final column list.
  3. Hidden-column types (state / request / result_spec) are not in this patch;
     they are created by the DDL path (rootserver/ob_ddl_service.cpp), not by
     the inner table definition.
